1.	Definitions:

a.	“Commercial Use” means your use for direct or indirect financial, commercial, or strategic gain or advantage, including without limitation: (a) bundling or integrating any SpliceAI2 Material with any hardware or software product for transfer, sale or license to a third party; (b) providing customers with access to any SpliceAI2 Material or Output for use with any hardware or software product purchased by that customer; (c) use in connection with the performance of services (including cloud computing services) for which you are compensated; and (d) creating publicly available tools or software, such as lookup tools, that use, incorporate, or otherwise rely on the SpliceAI2 Materials or Output.
b.	“Derivatives” means a modification or improvement created by or on behalf of you that directly modifies the source code, model architecture, or executable implementation of SpliceAI2.  Derivatives do not include Output or any independently developed software methods, models, tools, or other materials that do not incorporate, modify, or use the source code, model architecture, or executable implementation of SpliceAI2. 
c.	“Derivatives Patent” means any patent or patent application owned or controlled by, or otherwise licensable by, you that specifically claims or covers a Derivative.
d.	“Output” means the predictions and all related information provided by SpliceAI2 or otherwise using the SpliceAI2 Materials, together with any visual representations, computational predictions, descriptions, modifications, copies, or adaptations that are substantially derived from Output.  Notwithstanding the foregoing, Output does not include any modification, improvement, adaptation, or other material that incorporates, modifies, or enables reconstruction of any SpliceAI2 Materials, each of which constitutes a Derivative.
e.	“SpliceAI2 Information” means the model weights, precomputed scores, and any portion thereof, relating to SpliceAI2 that are made available by Illumina for use in accordance with this Agreement, together with (i) modifications to those weights and scores, (ii) works based on those weights and scores, or (iii) other code or machine learning models which incorporate, in full or in part, those weights and scores.  
f.	“SpliceAI2” means Illumina’s artificial intelligence model known as SpliceAI2, including the source code for such model.  
g.	“SpliceAI2 Materials” means, collectively, SpliceAI2 and the SpliceAI2 Information. 

